.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Vavilov found (1922-1927) that a dye&#x27;s fluorescence quantum yield does not change when it is excited at shorter, more energetic wavelengths. The reason is that ultrafast internal conversion carries any higher excited state down to S_1 before emission, so the yield depends only on the S_1 rate constants, \Phi_f=k_f/(k_f+k_{ic}+k_{isc}) (~chemistrykit.photochem.fluorescence_quantum_yield). Below, a model dye with an S_0\to S_1 band near 480 nm and an S_0\to S_2 band near 330 nm is excited across its whole absorption spectrum; kasha_emission_yields gives the S_1 fluorescence yield for each state reached.">

.. only:: html

